Modifications (CSSL section 5.2)
--------------------------------
Each modified file carries the notice "Modified by OpenMCX, <date of the change> (MCX N5 QoS)". The changes, as patches against
v2.2.1:

  patches/oai-cn5g-amf/   PDU Session Resource Modify Response: the failed PDU sessions (TS 38.413 9.2.1.6) go to
                          the SMF (PDU_RES_MOD_FAIL); the IEs are accepted whatever criticality the gNB sends
  patches/oai-cn5g-pcf/   N5 policy authorization: media components to PCC rules and QoS decisions (5QI 65 GBR),
                          PATCH and delete of app sessions, SmPolicyUpdateNotify; rule reports of the SMF notify
                          the AF (FAILED_RESOURCES_ALLOCATION)
  patches/oai-cn5g-smf/   PCF-initiated PDU session modification (TS 23.502 clause 4.3.3.2): QoS flow setup, change
                          and release; QoS flows the RAN refuses are released and reported (RES_ALLO_FAIL)
  patches/oai-cn5g-upf/   simple-switch keeps all PDRs of a session in the UL/DL lookups

Corresponding source
--------------------
The complete source of each image is the upstream repository at tag v2.2.1
(https://github.com/OPENAIRINTERFACE/oai-cn5g-<nf>, with its submodules) with the patches above applied:
build-images.sh recreates it and builds the images from it. The tag's commit of each network function is pinned
(README.md); each image names it, the submodule commits and the patches' SHA-256 in
/usr/share/doc/openmcx-oai/SOURCE. This also provides the source of the third-party
components the images contain, including those under the GPL-2.0 (UPF), the LGPL-2.1 or BSD-2-Clause, the MIT,
BSD-3-Clause and Apache-2.0 licenses.

Third-party notices
-------------------
Each image carries the network function's own NOTICE (/usr/share/doc/openmcx-oai/NOTICE.oai) and license texts
(/usr/share/doc/openmcx-oai/LICENSES/), unchanged from v2.2.1.

The other network functions of tutorial 3 (AUSF, NRF, UDM, UDR) and the RAN (gNB, nr-UE) are OAI's unmodified
images (oaisoftwarealliance/*), under their own licenses.
